{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SpinLabels","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SpinLabels","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.trivial_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.trivial_dim","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L76-L77","doc":"The trivial object has spin `0` and dimension `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.adjoint_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.adjoint_dim","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L73-L74","doc":"The adjoint object has spin `1` and dimension `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.fundamental_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.fundamental_dim","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L70-L71","doc":"The fundamental object has spin `1/2` and dimension `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjoint_is_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjoint_is_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L68-L68","doc":"`Ad(A) = V_1` (the spin-1 representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The adjoint object `Ad(A)` corresponds to spin `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamental_is_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamental_is_half","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L64-L64","doc":"`V = V_{1/2}` (the spin-1/2 representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamentalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamentalObj","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The fundamental object `V` corresponds to spin `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.simpleObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.simpleObj","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The simple object in `C` at spin label `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L50-L68","doc":"**Spin decomposition** in a QOU: the simple objects of `C` are\nindexed by `SpinLabels`, and the fundamental object has spin `1/2`.\n\nThis connects `SpinLabels` to the categorical framework: given a QOU,\nthe SU(2) emergence theorem forces the simple objects to be exactly\nthe spin-`j` representations.  The fundamental object `V` from the\nQOU has `j = 1/2` (categorical dimension 2). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spin-labels","label":"prop:spin-labels","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.cat_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.cat_dim","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L47-L48","doc":"The categorical dimension of `V_j` is `2j + 1 = twice_j + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.twice_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.twice_j","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The spin label `j`, represented as twice the spin (so `j = 0, 1, 2, 3, ...`\ncorresponds to spin `0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, ...`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinLabels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinLabels","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.lean#L33-L45","doc":"**Spin labels**: the simple objects of a quantum observable universe\nare indexed by half-integer spin labels `j ∈ {0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, ...}`,\nwith `V_j` having categorical dimension `2j + 1`.\n\nBy the SU(2) emergence theorem (`thm:su2-emergence`), the gauge group\nof any QOU is `SU(2)`, whose irreducible representations are exactly\nthe spin-`j` representations `V_j` with `dim V_j = 2j + 1`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:spin-labels}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}